From f91ecb0e64b769a971292e4a820b12ac308fdc21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: milliluk-erik <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:40:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/44] macosx: kAudioObjectPropertyElementMain, renamed in 12

kAudioObjectPropertyElementMaster was renamed to ...Main in macOS 12 and the
old spelling is deprecated, so every macOS build warns:

  ao_macosx.c:94: 'kAudioObjectPropertyElementMaster' is deprecated: first
                  deprecated in macOS 12.0

Use the new name, guarded so SDKs older than 12 -- which do not have it -- keep
building.

THE GUARD CANNOT BE #ifndef, and the first version of this patch got that wrong
in a way worth recording. The new name is an **enum constant**, not a macro, so
`#ifndef kAudioObjectPropertyElementMain` is true even on an SDK that defines
it. That version therefore defined the new name back to the deprecated one on
every system: the source read "Main", the compiler saw "Master", and the
warning it was written to remove survived it -- now pointing at the macro,
which is the only reason anyone noticed.

Gate on the SDK version instead. MAC_OS_VERSION_12_0 comes from
<AvailabilityMacros.h> and is defined only by SDKs new enough to have the
rename, which is exactly the condition being tested.

Upstream's warning, not ours; fixed here for the same reason as the texinfo
warnings in patch 3.
---
 src/macosx/ao_macosx.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/macosx/ao_macosx.c b/src/macosx/ao_macosx.c
index 259a307..f378785 100644
--- a/src/macosx/ao_macosx.c
+++ b/src/macosx/ao_macosx.c
@@ -30,6 +30,18 @@
 #include <string.h>
 
 #include <CoreAudio/AudioHardware.h>
+#include <AvailabilityMacros.h>
+
+// kAudioObjectPropertyElementMaster was renamed ...Main in macOS 12 and the
+// old spelling is deprecated.  The new name is an ENUM CONSTANT, not a macro,
+// so #ifndef cannot test for it -- an earlier attempt at this used #ifndef,
+// which is always true, and therefore #defined the new name back to the
+// deprecated one.  The code then read "Main" and compiled to "Master", and
+// the warning it was meant to remove survived it.  Gate on the SDK version
+// instead: MAC_OS_VERSION_12_0 is defined only by SDKs that have the rename.
+#if !defined(MAC_OS_VERSION_12_0)
+#define kAudioObjectPropertyElementMain kAudioObjectPropertyElementMaster
+#endif
 
 #include "xalloc.h"
 
@@ -91,7 +103,7 @@ static void *new(void *cfg) {
 
 	propertyAddress.mSelector = kAudioHardwarePropertyDefaultOutputDevice;
 	propertyAddress.mScope = kAudioObjectPropertyScopeGlobal;
-	propertyAddress.mElement = kAudioObjectPropertyElementMaster;
+	propertyAddress.mElement = kAudioObjectPropertyElementMain;
 
 	propertySize = sizeof(aomacosx->device);
 	if (AudioObjectGetPropertyData(kAudioObjectSystemObject, &propertyAddress, 0, NULL, &propertySize, &aomacosx->device) != noErr) {
